# Third-party licenses

`lyv` links the Rust crates listed below, including their build dependencies.
Every one is under a permissive license; none is copyleft. This file is generated —
`cargo about generate about.hbs -o THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md` — and regenerating it after
a dependency change is how a new obligation gets noticed.

Two things are **not** in this list and are worth stating:

- **SQLite** is compiled into the binary by `libsqlite3-sys`. Its C source is in the
  **public domain**, so it carries no attribution requirement at all. The Rust wrapper
  around it is MIT, and appears below.
- **`tippecanoe-decode`** is executed as a separate program by one test, which skips
  itself when the binary is absent. No code from it is linked or distributed, so it
  imposes nothing.

